    "explanation": "An affordance is a possibility for action created by the relationship between an object's or environment's features and an actor's abilities. A signifier indicates where or how to act. Effective design aligns perceptible cues with the action that is actually available. When form repeatedly invites the wrong behaviour, changing the object is often better than adding instructions.",
