    "explanation": "Tacit knowledge is practical understanding that cannot be fully encoded as rules or measurements. It appears in trained perception, timing, coordinated movement, and context-sensitive judgement. Records can preserve useful cues, but skill develops through demonstration, guided participation, comparison, feedback, and repeated practice. Tacit does not mean mystical or unteachable; it means that explicit instructions alone are insufficient.",
    "explanationZh": "默会知识是无法被规则和测量完全编码的实践理解，常表现为经过训练的感知、时机、动作协调与情境判断。记录能够保存线索，却不能独自替代示范、共同操作、比较、反馈和反复练习。“默会”并非神秘或不可教授，而是说明仅靠明文指令不足以形成熟练能力。"
