    "explanation": "Material affordance refers to the possibilities and resistances a material offers in relation to a purpose, tool, technique, force, and environment. Grain, hardness, moisture, and elasticity participate in what can be made, but do not dictate a single form. Skilled making tests and negotiates these properties rather than either obeying the material blindly or treating it as neutral matter.",
    "explanationZh": "材料可供性指材料在特定用途、工具、技术、受力与环境中提供的行动可能和阻力。纹理、硬度、含水量与弹性会参与成形，却不会命令唯一形式。熟练制作者通过测试与调整同材料协商，既不盲从材料，也不把它当作毫无差别的中性物。"
