    "explanation": "Theological hermeneutics examines how religious texts, doctrines, and traditions are understood and applied. It considers language, genre, historical setting, related texts, reception history, community practice, the interpreter's situation, and the consequences of a reading. Responsible interpretation neither repeats words as context-free commands nor permits arbitrary invention; it gives publicly accountable reasons for its choices.",
    "explanationZh": "神学诠释考察宗教文本、教义与传统如何被理解和应用，涉及语言、文体、历史语境、相关经典、接受史、共同体实践、解释者处境及解释后果。负责的诠释既不把文字逐字重复成脱离语境的命令，也不允许任意发挥，而要为取舍提供可公开检验的依据。"
