    "explanation": "Focalization concerns through whose perception or knowledge narrative information is selected: who can see, know, infer, or misunderstand what. It differs from who narrates. Internal, external, fixed, shifting, or multiple focalization changes information order, uncertainty, sympathy, and surprise; no single perspective automatically equals an objective whole.",
    "explanationZh": "叙事聚焦关注故事信息通过谁的感知或知识被选择，也就是谁能看见、知道、推断或误解什么；它不同于谁负责讲述。内部、外部、固定、切换或多重聚焦会改变信息顺序、不确定性、同情与惊奇，任何单一视角都不会自动等于客观全貌。"
