    "explanation": "Pragmatics studies how utterance meaning depends on context, speaker intention, shared knowledge, social relations, and listener inference. A statement may also perform a request, warning, complaint, or invitation. Inference is constrained by linguistic form and public evidence, not free guessing; when cues are insufficient or consequences are serious, clarification is more reliable than confidence.",
    "explanationZh": "语用学研究话语意义怎样依赖语境、说话者意图、共同知识、社会关系和听者推断。陈述句也可能实施请求、警告、抱怨或邀请。推断必须受语言形式与公开线索约束，并非任意猜测；当线索不足或后果重大时，澄清通常比自信猜测更可靠。"
