    "explanation": "A negative externality arises when an activity imposes costs on third parties who did not choose it and those losses are not fully included in the decision-maker's price. Private cost then understates social cost, so activity may be excessive. Regulation, charges, liability, bargaining, technology, or collective governance may help, each with measurement, enforcement, distributional, and irreversibility limits.",
