    "explanation": "Separation of powers allocates rule-making, execution, and adjudication among distinct institutions and uses checks to limit concentrated authority. It requires meaningful independence, information, resources, accountability, and defined coordination. Separation is not total isolation and may cause delay, so emergency powers need narrow scope, records, time limits, review, and remedies rather than unchecked consolidation.",
