    "explanation": "Cognitive dissonance is discomfort produced by inconsistency among important beliefs, commitments, actions, or evidence. People may reduce it by changing behaviour or belief, adding justifications, selecting information, or minimising the conflict. It is not identical to ordinary uncertainty or deliberate hypocrisy; it often operates while a person protects a valued self-image and prior decision.",
