    "explanation": "Norm enforcement maintains shared expectations through approval, reminders, shame, exclusion, punishment, or sanctions against those who fail to intervene, often without written law. Enforcement may be distributed among peers or organised formally. A persistent norm is not necessarily fair; power, visibility, and unequal ability to sanction shape who is constrained.",
    "explanationZh": "规范执行通过赞许、提醒、羞辱、排斥、惩罚或制裁不干预者来维持共同期待，往往无需成文法律。执行可以分散在同伴之间，也可能由正式机构承担。规范持续存在不代表它公平；权力、可见性和制裁能力会决定谁更容易被约束。"
