    "explanation": "Record version control identifies versions, states, and authority while governing approval, distribution, effective dates, supersession, and traceable change history. The newest copy may still be a draft, and an old version may remain necessary for audit or controlled rollback. Reliable control uses unique identifiers, permissions, receipts, change logs, authoritative sources, and explicit rules for offline copies.",
