    "explanation": "Inventory turnover measures how often average inventory is sold or used, commonly as cost of goods sold divided by average inventory; days inventory is its time-based counterpart. Low turnover may indicate excess, obsolescence, or holding cost, while very high turnover may reflect stockouts and underinvestment. Interpretation requires shelf life, replenishment time, margin, seasonality, and service goals.",
    "explanationZh": "库存周转常用销售成本除以平均库存，衡量库存被售出或使用的速度，库存天数则从时间角度表达。低周转可能意味着积压、过时与持有成本，过高也可能来自缺货和投入不足。解释时还须结合保质期、补货时间、利润、季节与服务目标。"
