    "explanation": "Dental caries is a dynamic, biofilm-mediated process. Frequent exposure to fermentable carbohydrates can shift the local ecology toward acid production, so demineralization exceeds remineralization. After individual assessment, some early non-cavitated lesions can be arrested or reversed through risk control, effective biofilm removal, fluoride-based measures, and monitoring; a cavitated or structurally compromised tooth may require restoration. The condition is not caused by a single bacterium, one sweet, or sugar quantity alone, and filling a defect does not by itself change the process that produced it. Management must be tailored to lesion activity, surface integrity, risk, and the patient.",
