    "explanation": "Occlusion concerns how upper and lower teeth relate in static contact and during jaw movement, together with loading of supporting tissues, muscles, temporomandibular joints, restorations, and neural adaptation. A bite-paper mark records contact, not force or an entire functional diagnosis. Relevant assessment can include symptoms, movement, loading, habits, tissue condition, and changes over time. Contact abnormalities may contribute to a problem, but they are not the sole explanation for all facial pain or headache. Irreversible adjustment needs a clear individualized basis and should preserve sound tooth structure whenever possible.",
    "explanationZh": "咬合涉及上下牙在静态接触和下颌运动中的关系，也牵涉支持组织、肌肉、颞下颌关节、修复体与神经适应。咬纸只记录接触，不能单独代表受力或诊断；评估还需结合运动、症状、习惯与时间变化。接触异常可能参与问题，却不能解释所有面部疼痛。不可逆调磨应有明确的个体化依据，并尽量保存健康牙体。"
