    "explanation": "Signal detection theory separates discriminability—how well signal and noise can be distinguished—from the decision criterion used to act under uncertainty. Lowering the criterion generally increases hits and false alarms; raising it reduces false alarms but increases misses. The appropriate criterion depends on prior probability, intended use, and the relative costs of errors. Better data quality, repeated observation, training, or independent review may improve discrimination rather than merely shifting the threshold. The four outcomes—hit, miss, false alarm, and correct rejection—should be examined together.",
    "explanationZh": "信号检测理论区分“辨别力”和“判定标准”：前者是信号与噪声能否分开，后者是在不确定下从何处采取行动。降低门槛通常同时增加命中与误报；提高门槛会减少误报，也增加漏报。标准应结合先验概率、用途及两类错误的代价。改善数据质量、重复观察、训练或独立复核可能提高辨别力，不能只靠移动阈值。命中、漏报、误报与正确排除应一起看。"
