    "explanation": "Neuroplasticity is the nervous system's capacity to change patterns of activity, connections, and functional organization with learning, experience, environment, or injury. Rehabilitation can use task-specific practice, repetition, salience, feedback, progression, variability, and adequate recovery, but effects depend on the person, lesion, timing, dose, and context. Gains may not transfer automatically from one trained measure to an untrained daily task, and plastic change can also support unhelpful patterns. The concept does not promise full recovery or imply that limited improvement reflects insufficient effort; assessment and training must be individualized.",
