    "explanation": "Positive youth development intentionally builds young people's strengths, agency, and contribution through supportive adult relationships, meaningful participation, skill development, safe opportunities, and enabling environments. It treats youth as partners rather than only as risks while retaining adult safeguarding responsibility. It complements prevention and specialist support without denying trauma, inequality, or danger or requiring every young person to succeed in one way.",
