    "explanation": "Motivational interviewing is a collaborative, goal-oriented communication style that uses partnership, acceptance, compassion, and careful listening to explore ambivalence, evoke the person's own reasons for change, and support autonomy. It has direction without argument, manipulation, or deciding for the person and can provide information with permission. It cannot replace emergency protection, practical resources, or other indicated treatment and support.",
