    "explanation": "Progressive overload gradually increases or changes training demands beyond the accustomed level to stimulate specific adaptation while balancing recovery, technique, goals, and individual response. Load can change through weight, repetitions, sets, speed, range, complexity, or frequency. It is not continuous maximal effort, a fixed progression formula, or permission to train through pain and danger signs.",
    "explanationZh": "渐进超负荷是逐步提高或改变训练要求，使刺激超过已适应水平并促成特异适应，同时同恢复、技术、目标和个体反应平衡。负荷可通过重量、次数、组数、速度、范围、复杂度或频率变化。它不是持续最大努力、固定增长公式，也不许可带着疼痛和危险警讯强行训练。"
